2791	2897	2942	2943	the priest	-1	“ I thank you for this beautiful ode ; the rose was always my idol flower ; in all its different stages of existence , it speaks a language my heart understands ; from its young bud ’s first crimson glow , to the last sickly blush of its faded blossom . It is the flower of sentiment in all its sweet transitions ; it breathes a moral , and seems to preserve an undecaying soul in that fragrant essence which still survives the bloom and symmetry of the fragile form which every beam too ardent , every gale too chill , injures and destroys . ”
